  "generated": "2026-11-12",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Salesforce Case alert rule versioning and activation semantics. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For a Case alert implemented as a Salesforce Flow, activating a new version automatically deactivates the previously active version. An already running Flow interview keeps the version with which it started. This is Flow behavior, not an established contract for an external Pub/Sub alert-rule engine. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_considerations_manage.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9b572fd2bfa2bb2cb88dcfef8df092e707fcc2de3dc472bd9ee317894d1ee0ec",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:730e8fd2908dd6d90f5d267c30fb07609320ffe72b6a8d1e64637f7348f1c230",
            "ev:f8f9fc3fc1f5c17caf05df454a184e51a593157a0533b35f60c2ed3e51a7395e"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=platform.flow_distribute_activate.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
            "https://salesforce.stackexchange.com/questions/419489/how-to-schedule-a-flow-version-activation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Production Flow deployment and activation are separate by default: change sets deploy flows deactivated even when active in the sandbox. Production settings can permit deployment of a new active version through change sets or Metadata API. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/flow-implementation-2/deploy-your-flow-to-production",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:085f5036531b751afedb7f2763f915b45eca761072368c4d7cc9a634dd194b17",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a16e7e35b3e5533819806e2caf6e8e4609ac1637ef0328add66247a2661e4e7e",
            "ev:cfcd49e45cdf62157dae02627b14d07b4f95958699946869f3d16cc867b7fe7b"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_considerations_manage.htm&language=en_US&type=5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For native Case escalation rules, activating a rule deactivates existing active escalation rules. Treat this as its own activation mechanism when choosing how to implement Case alerts. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://trailhead.salesforce.com/en/content/learn/modules/service_lex/service_lex_case_manage",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:cc54738aaa41ad4edc463b4da7d7bef1601fee9d9115184682a676211bd2be38",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:965421729df93f47d9ac1d15b0f15a69c5864ffa271bcbf39864eba3883761cf"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "JSBC Labs warns that reactivating an older Flow version can leave data writes, created records, scheduled actions or external-service effects from the newer version. Its recommendation is a release-level rollback plan that identifies compensation and irreversible external actions. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://jsbclabs.com/blog/activating-flow-version-is-not-release-management",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e8db54b6913e4250f63018680aec678fa38aa83911a66585e93345f8dfb68c91",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2c0499a8e25610820c36feb88fdcfe233eb2535e37dda6026815eacb6e9a02aa",
            "ev:fb40e3d52fed4769cfb54101c19980df3d8f085c0f9a8394296078886acba915"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "OrgTide describes editing an active Flow as creating a new version while the previously active version keeps running until explicit activation. Its guidance distinguishes saving a change from making that change live. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://orgtide.com/learn/salesforce-flow-versions",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:09db016aeb6f733358d73804a539ad495e78013789cd65c1719f39a853e93a59",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5e39eadb0fcdd647b68d43cb92678159a69fa1ab3c75572eb133adf6a57ca3b0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pending scheduled paths of a record-triggered Flow are a distinct case: pending automations use the currently active version when their scheduled time arrives. Do not assume that all deferred Case alerts remain pinned to the version active when queued. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_concepts_trigger_scheduled_path.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:32ca9c36a0cb4e5affbe8a4d4922c7d163d610cf3207070fd999590821472cb1",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3fd628e05f79e02992fb0568117d7bb83d4bfc7d6bedf4283f33607b8892a2a9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Deactivating a record-triggered Flow with scheduled paths does not immediately remove pending rows from the time-based automations list. Salesforce checks activation at their scheduled time and cancels pending automations if the Flow is then deactivated. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_concepts_trigger_scheduled_path.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:bf9477cbfec97ff2fc4fabaadb37fa0229c02bdc067449481bc69d6b6a6e5493",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3fd628e05f79e02992fb0568117d7bb83d4bfc7d6bedf4283f33607b8892a2a9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A new Flow version inherits the existing Flow’s runtime API version; Salesforce releases do not automatically advance that runtime API version. Treat a rule logic revision and a runtime API upgrade as separate changes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_ref_properties.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f0bf25943f4862e2d48c85e297df05f762940c45ae6c1298966923b0cb964139",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4224721f4a36d08972fb6f88ffa8995411dc283705649ab9da1a83269084b722"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Proposed application policy for an external Case-alert consumer: preserve immutable rule revisions, validate a candidate before activating it, and record an explicit activation boundary. Specify whether queued evaluations retain their assigned revision or resolve the active revision at execution. This is a design recommendation inferred from the different native Flow lifecycles, not a Salesforce Pub/Sub guarantee. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_considerations_manage.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6f96f899fdc7fddc98d9982de04459f3ab47f19622340b3cf51f8d1b2720da5e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:513404853f8f527073366747aa7977982b8eafbe766de6268ced57b777efd010",
            "ev:730e8fd2908dd6d90f5d267c30fb07609320ffe72b6a8d1e64637f7348f1c230",
            "ev:861fc779fd350323dae046825303bd19c7a07911197748560d9e609ff83d0bd9"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_concepts_trigger_scheduled_path.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
            "https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/flow-implementation-2/deploy-your-flow-to-production"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Before deleting an active Flow version, deactivate it. A Flow with paused interviews cannot be deleted until those interviews finish or are deleted. Retain the versions needed by those interviews during cleanup. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.flow_considerations_manage.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:cb69131f50f4d14d894f0dcc7658c436581b16a14bced350a8f5982ccc0b13c5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0d0f8671231dd4bfe3dbbaa742c049126507779caccbf29940c3eb9cc225a312"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Miguel Diaz initially reported that switching a screen Flow version would fail existing interviews, then corrected that premise in a July 2025 edit. This is a corrected community report, not evidence that activation normally breaks running interviews. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://salesforce.stackexchange.com/questions/419489/how-to-schedule-a-flow-version-activation",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4de012b3e1ed8f5e34f0905cd2595f130d999ed954d5ca709af876efe1bee0a2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
